body: "## Observed failure and impact\n\nPost-merge CI on `c4f8fd618805f1c9a3805a3ce7510d160c1ee07f` failed the Node 22 second release gate because the packed admission documentation fixture could not remove its temporary `global/locks` directory. The documented commands and assertions had already succeeded. This is an actionable test-lifecycle reliability issue: successful package behavior can still produce a red release gate.\n\nOfficial evidence: [run 42091355341, Node 22 job 127469923851](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/actions/runs/42091355341/job/127469923851). At 2026-11-05T19:17:08Z, the parent test reports the child command:\n\n`<runner tool cache>/node/22.23.4/x64/bin/node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/admission-docs-install.test.ts`\n\nChild stdout first prints `packed guide: 2 commands passed offline (JSON/TOON)` and the artifact SHA-512, then fails with:\n\n`ENOTEMPTY: directory not empty, rmdir '<runner temp dir>/jev-admission-docs-<temp>/global/locks'`\n\nThe parent test is `Node packed admission smoke stays offline and logs an explicit Bun skip without Bun in PATH`. It makes the second gate finish with 447 passed and 1 failed, despite 100% coverage. The first npm gate passed 448/448 and production audit reported zero vulnerabilities. Although the failing step is named “Full Bun release gate,” `release:check` invokes npm/Node coverage, and this nested test intentionally excludes Bun from PATH.\n\n## Exact source and expected behavior\n\n- [Packed documentation test lines 22–93](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/c4f8fd618805f1c9a3805a3ce7510d160c1ee07f/test/admission-docs-install.test.ts#L22-L93): the fixture isolates `PM_GLOBAL_PATH` under scratch, runs npm/npx commands sequentially, verifies JSON/TOON receipts and unchanged tracker state, then logs success at line 92. Line 93 closes the HTTP fixture and calls `rmSync(scratch, { recursive: true, force: true })` with no configured retries.\n- [Parent runner lines 109–125](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/c4f8fd618805f1c9a3805a3ce7510d160c1ee07f/test/admission-install-runner.test.ts#L109-L125): awaits the child process; its nonzero teardown result rejects before the explicit Bun-skip/output assertions.\n- [CI workflow](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/c4f8fd618805f1c9a3805a3ce7510d160c1ee07f/.github/workflows/ci.yml): Node 22/26 matrix, npm gate followed by Bun install and Bun-command gate.\n- Source goal: [pm-jev-tokenizer-admission](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/c4f8fd618805f1c9a3805a3ce7510d160c1ee07f/.agents/pm/features/pm-jev-tokenizer-admission.toon) and [merged PR #92](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/92) require offline installed-command proof and Node-only coverage when Bun is unavailable.\n\nExpected: successful packed-command behavior remains a successful test once owned resources are shut down and temporary artifacts are removed within a bounded cleanup policy. Persistent cleanup errors must remain visible. Actual: a directory removal error turns the otherwise successful smoke into a release-gate failure.\n\n## Investigation limits and ownership\n\nThis is one observed official Node 22 failure, not a deterministic local reproduction. Final PR CI and post-merge Node 26 passed. The merge commit has the same Git tree (`86fc209bbeb795d91122d2251a83971aed2a1a0b`) as final PR head `689ba33caaa0ad832d29ccd2c9aada9d9fc4d0ae`. This does not establish merge-introduced code drift or a Node 22-only defect.\n\nThe source/log establish the cleanup failure boundary, but do not identify which process or filesystem condition caused the directory to remain nonempty. A concurrent/late writer is a hypothesis, not a proven cause. No provider calls, dependency installation, broad local test rerun, or production mutation was performed for this investigation.\n\nDedup checked all 96 initial all-status Jev issue/PR records and refreshed all 97 before filing, all 53 canonical PM item records at the tested tree, all-status issue/PR searches for ENOTEMPTY/cleanup/flaky/admission-docs, relevant returned PR discussions, and PR #92 review threads. No matching Jev cleanup issue or explicit cleanup owner was found. The feature remains in progress but does not record this failure. Issues #93/#94 and the dev-glob advisory are separate.\n\nRelated precedent: [closed host chore pm-p5u6](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/chores/pm-p5u6.toon) handled resilient temporary-root cleanup in the host's packed-install workflow and older ENOTEMPTY incidents. Reuse its established lifecycle approach where appropriate; it does not currently fix this new Jev fixture.\n\n## Regression criteria\n\n1. Preserve the unchanged offline JSON/TOON commands, receipt checks, no-inference/no-mutation assertions, explicit Bun skip, artifact checks, and existing gate thresholds.\n2. Ensure owned processes/resources are finished before deletion; establish whether any child can outlive the awaited command before attributing the error to a particular producer.\n3. Add a focused deterministic teardown regression: a recoverable ENOTEMPTY condition is retried within a finite bound; an exhausted or unrelated cleanup error is surfaced. Do not blanket-ignore deletion errors or add unbounded sleeps.\n4. Verify focused packed documentation and Node-only runner tests, then both supported Node versions and existing npm/Bun-command gates on the final fix head. Record the exact head and results separately from this observed failure.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-05T19:40:59Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-jev#99 - Fix Tev1 admission references, Unicode regressions and smoke cleanup [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-12T11:58:30Z)\n>\n> Edited the description to name the runner tool cache and the runner temp directory instead of quoting their absolute paths. These were public CI paths, not private ones. The gated issue sync refuses absolute host paths in imported text (`absolute-host-path`, item `pm-jev-admission-teardown`), and this quote had blocked the daily pm-jev sync since 11-06."
